chapter.v:
Remove vexation 


from your, 


heart, and put away pain(3) from your body, for youth and the dawn of life are vanity. Footnotes (1) 11:5 Some Hebrew manuscripts, Targum; most Hebrew manuscripts *As you do not know the way of the wind, or how the bones grow in the womb* (2) 11:8 The Hebrew term *hebel* can refer to a “vapor” or “mere breath”; also verse 10 (see note on 1:2) (3) 11:10 Or *evil* (ESV)
